1. First, you'll need to create a bot and get its API token. You can follow this guide on how to create a bot: https://core.telegram.org/bots#3-how-do-i-create-a-bot

2. Install the `Telegram.Bot` NuGet package in your project:
```
Install-Package Telegram.Bot -Version 17.0.2
```

3. Make sure you have added the bot to the channels you want to listen to. The bot should have permission to read messages.

4. Now, you can use the following C# code to listen for incoming messages in those channels:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Threading;
using Telegram.Bot;
using Telegram.Bot.Args;

namespace TelegramChannelListener
{
    class Program
    {
        private static TelegramBotClient _telegramBotClient;

        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            // Replace with your API token
            string apiToken = "your_bot_token_here";
            _telegramBotClient = new TelegramBotClient(apiToken);

            _telegramBotClient.OnMessage += BotOnMessageReceived;
            _telegramBotClient.StartReceiving();

            // The listener will run indefinitely, so you can press Ctrl+C to stop the app
            Console.WriteLine("Bot is listening... Press any key to stop.");
            Console.ReadKey(true);

            _telegramBotClient.StopReceiving();
        }

        private static async void BotOnMessageReceived(object sender, MessageEventArgs messageEventArgs)
        {
            var message = messageEventArgs.Message;

            // Check if the message is from a channel
            if (message.Chat.Type == Telegram.Bot.Types.Enums.ChatType.Channel)
            {
                Console.WriteLine($"Message received in channel {message.Chat.Title}: {message.Text}");

                // You can perform any actions you want here, for example send a message to the channel
                // await _telegramBotClient.SendTextMessageAsync(message.Chat.Id, "Hello, I received your message!");
            }
        }
    }
}
```

Please note that this example is for monitoring channels using a bot account. It is not possible to monitor channels using your main account as a client, as the Telegram API doesn't support this functionality. You will have to use a bot account to achieve this.

